{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Yitro heard.</b> Rashi's comment: he heard about the splitting of the Sea of Reeds — as it is written, ״כי שמענו את אשר הוביש HaShem את מי ים סוף״. And since Yitro and Amalek are adjacent to each other, as it is written, ״ויאמר שאול אל הקיני סורו רדו מתוך עמלקי פן אוסיפך עמו״, now perhaps through fugitives who fled from the war with Amalek he heard." "<b>Yitro.</b> Rashi's comment: he had seven names. And if you ask: why does he not count Rekhav, since he too was called Yitro, as it is written, ״מבני רכב חותן משה״ — one may answer that Rashi counts here only those that were written in the Torah, but those from the words of the Prophets he does not count." "<b>Priest of Midian.</b> He was a great man, for Scripture equates him with Yavin, the associate — that is, Yitro, as it is written, ״כי שלום בין יבין מלך חצור ובין בית חבר הקיני״; from this we learn that he was a great man." "<b>Father-in-law of Moses.</b> Rashi's comment: here Yitro took pride in Moses — that is, here, now that Moses had grown great and become a prince, Yitro took pride in him; but previously, when he had not yet grown great and had fled from his land, Moses attributed greatness to his father-in-law, who was a prince in his city." "<b>All that Elohim had done for Moses.</b> That He saved him so that Pharaoh did not harm him, even though he was liable to the kingdom, and that He elevated him before Pharaoh and before his servants."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:26.430377248Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}